HOT SEAT
	SITUATIONAL JOURNAL
Deep work to reframe and resolve triggered emotions.
	

When to Use the Hot Seat
Use this whenever a situation, person, or thought has triggered a strong emotional response.
You will move from story to facts, from reaction to insight, from stuck to action.
	

What are you going to title this journal entry?




Who or what is the situation you are journaling about?




In this moment, why has that situation triggered you to complete this entry?






What is the STORY you are telling yourself about this situation?






List the single-word FEELINGS that arise when you tell yourself that story.






Describe any specific THOUGHTS and ACTIONS that arise when you tell yourself this story.






What EVIDENCE do you have to support this story as absolutely true?






What are the NON-EMOTIONAL FACTS about the situation?






What do you truly WANT for yourself in and beyond this situation?






What have you TRIED ALREADY to remedy or enhance this situation?






What WORKED and what did NOT WORK with that approach, and why?






What do you see as the REAL OBSTACLE or DISCOVERY in this moment?






What IDEAS do you have to solve or improve this situation that you have not yet tried?






Stepping back — why has this experience actually been POSITIVE for you?






Looking at how positive this has been, what is the simple LESSON on life you are taking from this?






What is the most significant INSIGHT you are leaving with, and why do you feel that way?






Compared to how you felt when you started — what singular words describe how you feel NOW?




What IMMEDIATE ACTIONS are you committed to take after leaving this entry?






